      answer: 0,
      why_en: "The mechanism is packing, and it is the whole content of FIGURE 10-1. In fully saturated compounds free rotation around each carbon-carbon bond gives the chain great flexibility, the most stable conformation is the fully extended form, and such molecules pack into nearly crystalline arrays with atoms along their lengths in van der Waals contact. A cis double bond forces a kink; kinked chains cannot pack as tightly and their interactions are weaker, so less thermal energy is needed to disorder the array (A p.343). Extend the same logic down TABLE 10-1 and it keeps working: 18:2 melts at minus 5, 18:3 at minus 11, and 20:4 at minus 49.5.",
      why_cn: "**机制是「堆积」**，这也是 **FIGURE 10-1 的全部内容**。在**完全饱和**的化合物里，**每根碳-碳键都能自由旋转**，链因此非常柔软，**最稳定的构象是完全伸展态**，这样的分子**叠成近乎晶体的阵列**，**整条链上的原子都处在范德华接触**中。**一个 cis 双键强行折出一个弯**；**弯了的链叠不紧、相互作用更弱**，因此**打乱这个阵列所需的热能更少**（ A 第 343 页）。**把同一套逻辑沿 TABLE 10-1 往下推，它一直成立**：**18:2 是 −5 ， 18:3 是 −11 ， 20:4 是 −49.5 。**"
