      why_en: "FIGURE 10-26's caption gives the reading rule explicitly and in order: “ The uniform series of ions 14 atomic mass units (u) apart represents loss of each successive methyl and methylene group from the methyl end of the acyl chain (beginning at C-18; the right end of the molecule as shown here), until the ion at m/z = 300 is reached. This is followed by a gap of 26 u for the carbons of the terminal double bond, at m/z = 274; a further gap of 14 u for the C-11 methylene group, at m/z = 260; and so forth. By this means, the entire structure is determined ” (A p.363). So runs of 14 are saturated stretches and a 26 marks a double bond. Note the limit the same caption states: “ although these data alone do not reveal the configuration (cis or trans) of the double bonds ” . The molecular ion at m/z 371 separately confirms a C18 acid with two double bonds.",
      why_cn: "**FIGURE 10-26 的图注把读法明确而有序地给了出来**：**「一串彼此相差 14 个原子质量单位（ u ）的均匀离子系列，代表从酰基链甲基端起（从 C-18 开始，即图中分子的右端）依次失去每一个甲基和亚甲基，直到到达 m/z = 300 那个离子。随后是一个 26 u 的间隔，对应末端双键的那两个碳，落在 m/z = 274 ；再往后又是一个 14 u 的间隔，对应 C-11 的亚甲基，落在 m/z = 260 ；如此类推。用这种办法，整个结构就被确定了。」**（ A 第 363 页）。**所以一连串 14 是饱和链段，而一个 26 标记一个双键。** **注意同一段图注给出的限度**：**「尽管仅凭这些数据，无法揭示双键的构型（ cis 还是 trans ）。」** **m/z 371 处的分子离子则单独确认这是一个带两个双键的 C18 酸。**"
