      options: [
        "Large proteins carry more charge and are pulled through the column faster",
        "The beads have cavities of a defined size: large proteins cannot enter them and take the short path around the beads, while small proteins enter and are slowed by a labyrinthine path through them",
        "Large proteins are denatured by the matrix and so pass through without interacting",
        "The gel acts as a sieve that physically retains small molecules in its pores by adsorption"
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why_en: "The column is a detour, not a filter. The stationary phase is cross-linked polymer beads with engineered pores of a particular size. Anything too large to enter a bead must travel around it — the short path — and so reaches the bottom sooner. Small proteins enter the cavities and are slowed by the more labyrinthine route. Lehninger itself calls the outcome 'a somewhat counterintuitive result', because the word sieve suggests the opposite. Note the contrast with polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis, where the gel really does act as a sieve in the ordinary sense and retards large molecules. Charge plays no part here (that is ion exchange), and nothing is denatured or adsorbed.",
      why_cn: "这根柱子是一条绕行路，不是一个过滤器。固定相是交联聚合物小球，内部有特定尺寸的孔隙。凡是大到进不去小球的分子，都必须绕着小球走——那是近路——因此更早到达柱底。小蛋白则进入空腔，被更加迷宫化的路径拖慢。 Lehninger 自己把这个结果称为「一个多少有点反直觉的结果」，因为「筛子」这个词给人的印象恰好相反。请注意它与聚丙烯酰胺凝胶电泳的对比：在电泳中凝胶确实是通常意义上的筛子，会阻滞大分子。电荷在这里不起作用（那是离子交换的事），也没有什么被变性或吸附。"
