      options: [
        "It is not central; it is a historical method retained only for teaching",
        "It is analytical rather than preparative: it lets you rapidly estimate how many proteins are in a mixture, judge the purity of a preparation, and determine pI and approximate molecular weight — and one of the two criteria for calling a protein pure is that only a single species is detectable on an SDS gel",
        "It is the only method that can separate proteins of identical size",
        "It concentrates the protein, which is necessary before the assay can be performed"
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why_en: "Electrophoresis is a way of looking, not a way of making, and Lehninger is unusually candid that it often adversely affects protein structure and function. Its value is that it answers questions the preparative steps cannot: how many different proteins remain, how pure the preparation is, what the pI and approximate molecular weight are. It also supplies half the operational definition of purity — a protein is considered pure when further steps fail to raise specific activity AND only a single species can be detected, for example by SDS gel electrophoresis. Those are two independent criteria, one functional and one physical, and electrophoresis provides the physical one. It does not concentrate anything.",
      why_cn: "电泳是一种「看」的手段，而不是「造」的手段； Lehninger 也异常坦率地指出它常常对蛋白的结构和功能产生不利影响。它的价值在于回答那些制备性步骤无法回答的问题：还剩下多少种不同的蛋白、制备物有多纯、 pI 和近似分子量是多少。它同时还提供了「纯」这一操作性定义的一半——当进一步的步骤不再能提高比活性，并且只能检测到单一物种（例如通过 SDS 凝胶电泳）时，才认为蛋白是纯的。这是两条互相独立的判据，一条功能上的、一条物理上的，而电泳提供的是物理那一条。它并不起浓缩作用。"
