      answer: 1,
      why_en: "Two effects fight each other in any column. Resolution improves as the column gets longer, because the proteins have more distance in which to separate; but every band also broadens with time through diffusional spreading, which degrades resolution. HPLC attacks the second term rather than the first: high-pressure pumps speed the molecules down the column and higher-quality matrix materials withstand the crushing force, so transit time falls and diffusion has less time to act. Option A is the trap — column length does raise resolution, but that is not what HPLC changes, and simply lengthening the column also gives diffusion longer to work.",
      why_cn: "在任何一根柱子里都有两种效应在互相对抗。柱子越长分辨率越高，因为蛋白有更多距离可以拉开；但每一条带也会因扩散扩宽而随时间变宽，从而降低分辨率。 HPLC 对付的是后一项而不是前一项：高压泵加快分子沿柱下行的速度，更高品质、能承受压力的基质材料使之可行，于是停留时间缩短，扩散作用的时间也随之减少。选项 A 是陷阱——柱长确实能提高分辨率，但那不是 HPLC 所改变的东西，而且单纯加长柱子也会让扩散有更长的时间发挥作用。"
