      answer: 3,
      why_en: "An uncompetitive inhibitor “binds only to the ES complex”, so it deletes ES rather than free enzyme. Vmax falls because there is effectively less enzyme; apparent Km falls by exactly the same factor, because “only ES (not free enzyme) is deleted from the reaction”, so less substrate is needed to reach half of the new, lower ceiling (A p.199). Both intercepts move and the slope does not, which is why “the lines generated in the presence and absence of an inhibitor are parallel” — always above the uninhibited line (A p.198).",
      why_cn: "反竞争性抑制剂**只结合 ES 复合物**，所以它删掉的是 ES ，不是游离酶。 Vmax 下降，因为实际可用的酶变少了；表观 Km **按完全相同的因子**下降，因为**被删掉的只有 ES ，不是游离酶**，于是达到那个新的、更低的天花板的一半所需的底物也更少（ A 印刷页 199 ）。两个截距都动而斜率不动，这就是为什么**有抑制剂与无抑制剂的两条直线是平行的**——而且总在无抑制线的上方（ A 印刷页 198 ）。"
