  quiz: [
    { type: 'mcq',
      q_en: "Why is citrate an especially well-chosen allosteric activator of acetyl-CoA carboxylase?",
      q_cn: "为什么柠檬酸作为乙酰辅酶 A 羧化酶的变构激活剂是一个特别恰当的选择？",
      options: [
        "Because citrate is the immediate product of the carboxylase reaction, giving direct product feedback",
        "Because citrate is simultaneously the vehicle carrying acetyl groups out of the mitochondrion and the signal activating the enzyme that consumes them, so a rising supply is its own 'go' signal",
        "Because citrate is the only metabolite able to cross the inner mitochondrial membrane",
        "Because citrate inhibits AMP-activated protein kinase, preventing phosphorylation of the carboxylase"
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why_en: "Acetyl-CoA cannot cross the inner mitochondrial membrane, so it leaves as citrate; in the cytosol citrate lyase regenerates acetyl-CoA. Citrate is therefore the delivery vehicle for the substrate AND, by raising the carboxylase's Vmax, the activation signal — when mitochondrial acetyl-CoA and ATP are plentiful, the same molecule both supplies and switches on the pathway. Citrate is not the carboxylase's product (malonyl-CoA is), and other metabolites cross the membrane on their own transporters.",
      why_cn: "乙酰辅酶 A 无法穿过线粒体内膜，因此以柠檬酸的形式离开；在胞质中由柠檬酸裂解酶重新生成乙酰辅酶 A 。所以柠檬酸既是底物的运输载体，又通过提高羧化酶的 Vmax 而成为激活信号——当线粒体内乙酰辅酶 A 和 ATP 充裕时，同一个分子既供料又开启该途径。柠檬酸并不是羧化酶的产物（产物是丙二酰辅酶 A ），而其他代谢物也各有自己的转运体可跨膜。"
    },
    { type: 'mcq',
      q_en: "Why are linoleate and alpha-linolenate essential fatty acids for mammals?",
      q_cn: "为什么亚油酸和α-亚麻酸对哺乳动物是必需脂肪酸？",
      options: [
        "Mammals lack fatty acid synthase and so cannot make any fatty acid longer than 16 carbons",
        "Mammals cannot introduce a double bond beyond carbon 9 of the chain, so these polyunsaturated acids must come from dietary plant material",
        "They are destroyed by beta-oxidation as fast as they are made, so a dietary supply is needed to maintain the level",
        "They can only be made in the chloroplast, an organelle mammals possess but cannot activate"
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why_en: "Mammalian desaturases can place a cis double bond at C-9 — giving palmitoleate and oleate from palmitate and stearate — but cannot desaturate beyond C-9. Linoleate (18:2) and alpha-linolenate (18:3) therefore cannot be synthesised at all and must be obtained from plants. This matters downstream: linoleate is the sole route to arachidonate, and hence to the series 2 eicosanoids, while alpha-linolenate gives EPA and DHA.",
      why_cn: "哺乳动物的去饱和酶可以在 C-9 处引入一个顺式双键——从软脂酸和硬脂酸分别生成棕榈油酸和油酸——但无法在 C-9 之后进行去饱和。因此亚油酸（ 18:2 ）和α-亚麻酸（ 18:3 ）根本无法合成，必须从植物获取。这在下游很重要：亚油酸是通往花生四烯酸、进而通往 2 系列类二十烷酸的唯一途径，而α-亚麻酸则生成 EPA 和 DHA 。"
    },
    { type: 'mcq',
      q_en: "Aspirin relieves inflammatory pain and, at low regular doses, reduces heart attack risk — yet it does not help asthma. What explains all three facts?",
      q_cn: "阿司匹林能缓解炎性疼痛，低剂量长期服用还能降低心梗风险，却对哮喘无效。什么能同时解释这三个事实？",
      options: [
        "Aspirin inhibits phospholipase A2, so no arachidonate is released for any downstream pathway",
        "Aspirin acetylates a Ser residue in both COX isozymes, blocking prostaglandin and thromboxane synthesis, but the lipoxygenase route to leukotrienes is not inhibited by NSAIDs",
        "Aspirin selectively inhibits COX-2 only, leaving COX-1 and all leukotriene synthesis untouched",
        "Aspirin blocks thromboxane synthase directly, and prostaglandin effects are only an indirect consequence"
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why_en: "Aspirin irreversibly acetylates a Ser residue in the active site of both COX-1 and COX-2. Losing COX-2-derived prostaglandins relieves inflammation, pain and fever; losing platelet thromboxane A2 reduces aggregation and vasoconstriction, which is the basis of low-dose prophylaxis. But leukotrienes are made by lipoxygenases on the separate 'linear' branch, which aspirin and other NSAIDs do not inhibit — and since leukotrienes mediate bronchoconstriction, asthma is unaffected.",
      why_cn: "阿司匹林不可逆地乙酰化 COX-1 和 COX-2 活性位点上的一个丝氨酸残基。失去 COX-2 来源的前列腺素可缓解炎症、疼痛和发热；失去血小板的血栓烷 A2 则减少聚集和血管收缩，这正是低剂量预防用药的依据。但白三烯是由脂氧合酶在另一条「线式」分支上生成的，阿司匹林和其他非甾体抗炎药并不抑制该分支——而白三烯介导支气管收缩，所以哮喘不受影响。"
    },
    { type: 'short',
      q_en: "Acetyl-CoA is made inside mitochondria but fatty acids are built in the cytosol. Explain how the acetyl groups get out, and where the NADPH for synthesis comes from.",
      q_cn: "乙酰辅酶 A 在线粒体内生成，而脂肪酸在胞质中合成。请解释乙酰基如何离开线粒体，以及合成所需的 NADPH 从何而来。",
      accept: ["citrate", "citrate lyase", "malic enzyme", "pentose phosphate", "malate", "柠檬酸", "裂解酶", "苹果酸酶", "磷酸戊糖", "苹果酸"],
      answer_en: "See source node L-21-1-1.",
      answer_cn: "线粒体内膜对乙酰辅酶 A 不通透，因此乙酰基以柠檬酸的形式离开。在线粒体内，乙酰辅酶 A 经柠檬酸合酶与草酰乙酸缩合生成柠檬酸；柠檬酸经柠檬酸转运体跨膜；在胞质中，柠檬酸裂解酶消耗一个 ATP 将其重新裂解为乙酰辅酶 A 和草酰乙酸。草酰乙酸无法直接返回，因为不存在草酰乙酸转运体，于是它被胞质苹果酸脱氢酶还原为苹果酸，苹果酸再由苹果酸酶转化为丙酮酸和 CO2 ，并生成 NADPH 。这条路线提供脂肪酸合成所需 NADPH 的约一半，其余由磷酸戊糖途径提供。胞质中很高的 [NADPH]/[NADP+] 比值（肝细胞中约为 75 ）为该途径提供了所需的还原性环境。"
    }
  ],
