      why_en: "Both framings are true and an exam answer should hold both. The pathology is right: uncontrolled production causes acidosis, ketosis and can kill. But the same molecules are a normal, quantitatively major inter-organ fuel. The decisive property is that ketone bodies cross the blood-brain barrier while fatty acids do not, so converting fat into a small water-soluble acid is the only way body fat can reach the brain at all. That is what allows a fasting human to stay conscious and spares muscle protein until severe starvation. Option C is wrong — the liver makes them, which the Czech account states correctly. Acetone is the minor, non-metabolisable one, so D is inverted.",
      why_cn: "两种框架都成立，考试作答时应同时握住。病理那一面是对的：失控的生成会导致酸中毒、酮症，甚至致命。但同样这些分子也是一种正常的、在数量上举足轻重的器官间燃料。决定性的性质在于酮体能穿过血脑屏障而脂肪酸不能，所以把脂肪转化为一种小分子水溶性酸，是体脂能够抵达大脑的唯一途径。正是它让禁食中的人保持清醒，并为肌肉蛋白争取缓冲，直到严重饥饿为止。选项 C 错误——酮体由肝脏生成，这一点捷克教材说得没错。丙酮是次要的、不能被代谢利用的那一个，所以 D 把关系弄反了。"
