        "The cycle stores ATP as phosphocreatine; glyceroneogenesis regenerates NADPH for fatty acid synthesis",
        "The cycle is genuinely futile and is regarded as a pathological feature of obesity; glyceroneogenesis is the pathway that removes excess glycerol"
