      answer: 1,
      why_en: "Strand separation at the origin is mechanical, not enzymatic. Eight DnaA molecules, all ATP-bound, assemble on the R and I sites into a right-handed helical complex; the DNA wraps tightly around it and this introduces a positive supercoil. The resulting strain, helped by further DnaA binding at the DUE, is what opens the helix, and the A=T-rich DUE gives way first because AT pairs are the easiest to separate. DnaB comes AFTER this: it is loaded by DnaC into the already-denatured region, and that loading is the key step of initiation. Gyrase relieves stress ahead of the fork rather than opening the origin, and Dam methylation is part of the once-per-cycle timer.",
      why_cn: "起点处的链分离是力学过程，而非酶促过程。八个全部结合 ATP 的 DnaA 分子在 R 位点和 I 位点上组装成右手螺旋复合体； DNA 紧密缠绕其上，从而引入一个正超螺旋。由此产生的张力，加上更多 DnaA 结合到 DUE 区域，才是把双螺旋打开的原因；而富含 A=T 的 DUE 之所以最先屈服，是因为 AT 配对最容易分开。 DnaB 是在这之后才登场的：它由 DnaC 装载到已经变性的区域中，而这一装载正是起始阶段的关键步骤。旋转酶负责消除复制叉前方的张力，而不是打开起点； Dam 甲基化则属于「每周期一次」的计时机制。"
